     "explanation": "This is **liaison**: a silent final consonant revives before a vowel and attaches to the next word, and a revived s is pronounced z. Elision is the other phenomenon — a dropped vowel with an apostrophe, as in **j'ai**. Nothing changes in the spelling: **vous avez** is written the same whether or not you hear the link.",
